# Components

Reusable UI components live here.

## Rules

- Every component should be focused and small (single responsibility).
- Components must not contain business logic or API calls directly.
- Use `hooks/` for state and side effects.
- Use `services/` for API calls.

## Component Structure

```
components/
  ComponentName/
    ComponentName.tsx       # Component implementation
    ComponentName.module.css # Component styles
    ComponentName.test.tsx  # Component tests
    index.ts                # Barrel export
```

## Naming

- PascalCase for component names and files.
- Describe what the component IS, not what it does.
  - ✅ `UserCard`, `LoadingSpinner`, `ErrorBanner`
  - ❌ `showUser`, `spinner`, `displayError`

## Required UI States

Every data-driven component must handle:

```tsx
if (loading) return <LoadingSpinner />;
if (error)   return <ErrorBanner message={error} />;
if (!data)   return <EmptyState message="No items found" />;
return <SuccessContent data={data} />;
```

---

*Components will be created after Phase 0 analysis identifies the UI requirements.*
